      // ABOUT
      'about.eyebrow': 'About Letterhome',
      'about.h1': 'A small mail service, run from Canada.',
      'about.p': 'Letterhome prints and posts letters and documents from inside Canada on your behalf. Each order is checked for obvious problems, printed in black & white by default (colour available), sealed in an envelope with Canadian postage, and handed to Canada Post.',
      'about.cta.send': 'Send a letter',
      'about.cta.contact': 'Get in touch',
      'about.story.eyebrow': 'Why we built this',
      'about.story.h2': 'The gap we\'re filling.',
      'about.story.p1': 'If you live outside Canada, mailing something back home is harder than it should be. The CRA wants signed paper. Family expect a letter on the right day. Banks and accountants keep sending mail to addresses you no longer use. From Berlin, Bangkok or Auckland, none of that is easy to deal with.',
      'about.story.p2': 'Letterhome is the workaround. You write the letter, attach any documents, pay, and we mail it from Canada, just like dropping it off at a Canada Post box yourself. We also mail outwards from Canada to 160+ countries, so it works the other way around too.',
      'about.story.p3': 'Orders are checked before printing for things that would stop delivery, such as bad addresses and unreadable PDFs. A simple automatic check on our own server also looks for illegal content. We do not read or share what you wrote unless that check flags it. You can ask us to delete your letter and personal information at any time.',
      'about.manifesto': 'A small operation, run from Canada. Every order is checked before it goes in the post.',
      'about.values.h2': 'How we operate.',
      'about.v01.h3': 'Checked before printing',
      'about.v01.p': 'Every order is checked before printing for addressing errors, unreadable attachments, or anything else that would stop the mail from getting through. If there\'s a problem, we email you before charging or printing.',
      'about.v02.h3': 'We don\'t keep your letters',
      'about.v02.p': 'You can ask us to delete your letter and personal information at any time. We keep a basic order record, date, amount, your email, for Canadian tax purposes. Not what you wrote.',
      'about.v03.h3': 'Flat pricing',
      'about.v03.p': '$6 to an address in Canada or the United States, $9 to the UK or Australia, $15 to anywhere else. The price includes the first 2 pages, the envelope, postage, and the trip to the post office. Black & white printing is included by default; colour is $1, and each page after the first 2 is $0.55 ($0.75 in colour).',
      'about.v04.h3': 'Payments through Stripe',
      'about.v04.p': 'Payments are processed by Stripe. We don\'t see or store your card details, and your financial information doesn\'t touch our systems.',
      'about.v05.h3': 'Canada Post for delivery',
      'about.v05.p': 'Letters go through Canada Post\'s network with the same postage and service level you\'d get if you\'d mailed it yourself from a Canadian address.',
      'about.v06.h3': 'Direct replies',
      'about.v06.p': 'No ticket queues. If something goes wrong with your order, the person who replies is the person who handled it. We aim to respond within one business day.',
      'about.cta.h2': 'Ready to send one?',
      'about.cta.p': 'Write your letter, attach any documents, and pay. We\'ll mail it from Canada within two business days.',
      'about.cta.btn': 'Send a letter, from $6',
